<h1>Check in from the edge</h1>
<p class="lead">This page keeps its data in <strong>Cloudflare D1</strong>, the SQLite
Cloudflare runs next to the Worker. Press the button: the Worker that answers stores the
datacenter and the country it served you from — nothing that identifies you.</p>

<form method="post" action="/d1/check-in" class="check-in">
  <button class="button" type="submit">Check in from <%= @runtime["colo"] %></button>
  <% if @checked_in %>
    <span class="notice">Stored in D1 ✓</span>
  <% end %>
  <% if @busy %>
    <span class="muted">Busy: 30 check-ins this minute already. Try again in a moment.</span>
  <% end %>
</form>

<div class="stats">
  <div><span><%= @total %></span> check-ins</div>
  <div><span><%= @colos %></span> datacenters</div>
  <div><span><%= @db_ms %> ms</span> in D1 for this page</div>
</div>

<div class="grid two">
  <section>
    <h2>By datacenter</h2>
    <% if @by_colo.length > 0 %>
      <ol class="ranking">
        <% @by_colo.each do |row| %>
          <li><code><%= row["colo"] %></code> × <%= row["n"] %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ol>
    <% else %>
      <p>Nobody yet. Be the first.</p>
    <% end %>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Latest</h2>
    <table class="list">
      <% @latest.each do |check_in| %>
        <tr>
          <td><code><%= check_in.colo %></code></td>
          <td><%= check_in.country %></td>
          <td class="muted"><%= check_in.at %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </table>
  </section>
</div>

<h2>The code</h2>
<p>An ordinary model and controller. Nothing here knows it runs on the edge; the
adapter comes from <code>wrangler.toml</code>.</p>
<pre><code class="language-soli">class CheckIn &lt; Model
  validates("colo", {"presence": true, "max_length": 8})
end

# GET /d1
def index(req)
  per_colo = CheckIn.group_by("colo").all.sort_by { |row| -row["n"] }
  @total = per_colo.reduce(fn(sum, row) sum + row["n"], 0)
  @by_colo = per_colo.take(12)
  @latest = CheckIn.order("at", "desc").limit(10).all
end

# POST /d1/check-in
def create(req)
  CheckIn.create({"colo": req["headers"]["cf-colo"], "country": …, "at": …})
  redirect("/d1?checked_in=1")
end</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-toml">[[d1_databases]]
binding = "DB"
database_name = "soli-cf-demo"
database_id = "…"

[vars]
SOLI_DB_ADAPTER = "d1"</code></pre>
<p>Each statement is a round trip from the Worker to D1, and the interpreter's stack
is suspended while it waits (JavaScript Promise Integration). See the
<a href="/guide">guide</a> to set it up.</p>
